{"name":"Monet Vert","hex":"#92dbc4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vert","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A green colour, now only in heraldry; represented in engraving by diagonal parallel lines 45 degrees counter-clockwise.","Green undergrowth or other vegetation growing in a forest, as a potential cover for deer."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In blazon, of the colour green."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vert"}],"entries":[{"title":"Claude Monet","blocks":[{"text":"Oscar-Claude Monet was a French painter and founder of Impressionism who is seen as a key precursor to modernism, especially in his attempts to paint nature as he perceived it. During his long career, he was the most consistent and prolific practitioner of Impressionism's philosophy of expressing one's perceptions of nature, especially as applied to plein air (outdoor) landscape painting. The term \"Impressionism\" is derived from the title of his painting Impression, Sunrise, which was exhibited in 1874 at the First Impressionist Exhibition, initiated by Monet and a number of like-minded artists as an alternative to the Salon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Claude_Monet_1899_Nadar_crop.jpg/330px-Claude_Monet_1899_Nadar_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Monet","wikidata":"Q296"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG/500px-Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG/1280px-Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG/500px-Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG?utm_source=en